<div class="support-ask">
  <p>I'm asking for money to keep this research running. Not for a promise about what it will become.</p>
  <p>What it covers: a laptop and a phone that can compile and run the models I've built, instead of a budget Android. Cloud compute and API credits for the agent and dialogue instruments. Transport and power to keep working from where I actually am. Some of it pays for the community work in Berkeley, in cash, to the people doing it.</p>
  <p>The floor is a few thousand dollars, which buys stability this month. $40,000 buys a working development environment. $80,000 is a year of full-time building.</p>
  <p>At $200,000, the Berkeley pilot runs and produces evidence for whether any of this scales.</p>
  <p>I'm not offering equity, a roadmap, or governance. What I can offer is the record: an append-only builder journal, published code, and instruments you can run yourself and disagree with.</p>
